config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_MCU_WDT
	bool "thingino-mcu-wdt"
	help
	  Disables the hardware watchdog on a discrete companion MCU (found on
	  some Ingenic camera boards, e.g. the MindMotion MM32F0020B1T on the
	  Cinnado B6 T23ZN/TM18NA LTE variant) as early as possible during boot.

	  On boards where this MCU is present, its watchdog can power-cycle the
	  whole SoC if not disabled quickly after boot. This package ships the
	  vendor's own extracted disable-watchdog tool (a small prebuilt uClibc/
	  MIPS binary that pulses a wake GPIO and sends the disable command over
	  I2C) and runs it from the earliest available init hook (an F-prefixed
	  script in /etc/init.d, run by rcF before rcS), rather than reimplementing
	  the I2C wire protocol from scratch.

	  Only enable this for boards that actually have this MCU wired up.

	  NOTE: unlike package/atbm6461-tools (which rebuilds its vendor tool
	  from source against an extracted librtos.so), this package ships the
	  vendor binary wholesale, because disable_mcu_wdt has no shared-library
	  dependency to link against -- its I2C packet framing (magic/CRC) is
	  statically compiled into the binary itself and hasn't been fully
	  decoded yet. Once it is, reworking this into a source-built tool
	  (matching the atbm6461-tools pattern) would be the more idiomatic
	  long-term fix.
